  "worked_solution": "To find the complex conjugate, we flip the sign of the imaginary part.\n\nIn the given number $z=11\\text{i},$ the imaginary part is $11\\text{i}$ (there is no real part, just an imaginary part). Flipping the sign, we get $-11\\text{i}.$\n\nTherefore, the complex conjugate is given by $\\overset{\u2015}{z}=-11\\text{i}.$",
